From d473432a2f93398c55ad9524c41b59c06a3e21da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: scholzri <33288574+scholzri@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 19:03:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] usb: device: cdc_acm: set the call management data interface

cdc_interface_config() renumbers a CDC ACM function when it is not the
first one in the configuration: interface numbers, the union
descriptor and the IAD. The Call Management functional descriptor kept
its static bDataInterface = 1, so every CDC ACM port after the first
pointed at the wrong data interface (seen as bDataInterface 1 on a
second port at interfaces 3/4). Linux uses the union descriptor and
does not notice; hosts that read the Call Management descriptor get a
wrong data interface. Set it with the other interface numbers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 subsys/usb/device/class/cdc_acm.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/subsys/usb/device/class/cdc_acm.c b/subsys/usb/device/class/cdc_acm.c
index 66c098f933..02e9bd6e8d 100644
--- a/subsys/usb/device/class/cdc_acm.c
+++ b/subsys/usb/device/class/cdc_acm.c
@@ -486,6 +486,7 @@ static void cdc_interface_config(struct usb_desc_header *head,
 
 	desc->if0.bInterfaceNumber = bInterfaceNumber;
 	desc->if0_union.bControlInterface = bInterfaceNumber;
+	desc->if0_cm.bDataInterface = bInterfaceNumber + 1;
 	desc->if1.bInterfaceNumber = bInterfaceNumber + 1;
 	desc->if0_union.bSubordinateInterface0 = bInterfaceNumber + 1;
 	desc->iad_cdc.bFirstInterface = bInterfaceNumber;
-- 
